      "id": 1,
      "text": "Peterson was named for Adlie Peterson, an early settler who helped establish the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peterson%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Peterson was platted in 1881 when the railroad was extended to that point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peterson%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1862, settlers built a fort in Peterson to defend against anticipated Dakota attacks during the Dakota War, though it was never attacked.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peterson%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Kirchner Farm Museum, Jim's History Barn, and the French Museum showcase Peterson’s rich pioneer heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.traveliowa.com/cities/peterson-iowa/180/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Inkpaduta’s band of Native Americans visited the Kirchners on November 23, 1856, and again on February 14, 1857, before heading north to Spirit Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
